[[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NVIDIA/NVFlare/issues/comments/4984224473","html_url":"https://github.com/NVIDIA/NVFlare/issues/4908#issuecomment-4984224473","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NVIDIA/NVFlare/issues/4908","id":4984224473,"node_id":"IC_kwDOFy3KIc8AAAABKRU62Q","user":{"login":"pcnudde","id":1881453,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4ODE0NTM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1881453?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pcnudde","html_url":"https://github.com/pcnudde","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pcnudde/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pcnudde/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pcnudde/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pcnudde/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pcnudde/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pcnudde/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pcnudde/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pcnudde/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pcnudde/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-15T18:54:17Z","updated_at":"2026-07-15T18:54:17Z","body":"Thanks for the detailed write-up — this is an important use case for us. In the upcoming 2.9 release we are making Slurm a first-class deployment target alongside Docker and Kubernetes. That said, the two constraints you describe are cluster policies the integration itself cannot remove — the client process still needs to run somewhere persistent with a network path to the FL server.\n\nOur normal recommendation is a variant of your Option 2: run the client on a service/workflow node rather than a login node. Many centers can provide one for persistent orchestration processes (the same class as Nextflow/Snakemake head processes). The client is lightweight — no GPU; it only needs shared-filesystem access, the Slurm submit tools, and outbound connectivity to the server.\n\nOn Option 1: does your center provide a proxy or gateway that allows network egress from compute nodes to approved external destinations? If so, running the client as a long-lived Slurm job can work — it needs a single outbound TCP connection to one host/port, which is usually easy to allowlist. Happy to go into details if that path is available to you.","author_association":"COLLABORATOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NVIDIA/NVFlare/issues/comments/4984224473/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"pcnudde","id":1881453,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4ODE0NTM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1881453?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pcnudde","html_url":"https://github.com/pcnudde","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pcnudde/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pcnudde/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pcnudde/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pcnudde/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pcnudde/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pcnudde/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pcnudde/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pcnudde/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pcnudde/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NVIDIA/NVFlare/issues/comments/4992571484","html_url":"https://github.com/NVIDIA/NVFlare/issues/4908#issuecomment-4992571484","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NVIDIA/NVFlare/issues/4908","id":4992571484,"node_id":"IC_kwDOFy3KIc8AAAABKZSYXA","user":{"login":"falibabaei","id":66964597,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY2OTY0NTk3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/66964597?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/falibabaei","html_url":"https://github.com/falibabaei","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/falibabaei/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/falibabaei/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/falibabaei/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/falibabaei/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/falibabaei/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/falibabaei/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/falibabaei/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/falibabaei/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/falibabaei/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-16T13:39:33Z","updated_at":"2026-07-16T13:39:33Z","body":"Dear @pcnudde,\n\nThank you very much for the quick reply. I have already tested both approaches on one HPC system, and both worked well. However, my goal is to find a more general solution that can be applied across different HPC centers, each with its own policies and operational constraints.\n\nFor **Option 2**, I have a working example using a custom Slurm launcher here which worked for me in the simulation mode:\n\n- https://github.com/falibabaei/nvflare-hello-pt-slurm/tree/main\n\nThe main challenge I've encountered is that not every HPC center provides a persistent service/workflow node for users.\n\nRegarding **Option 1**, I agree that allowing a single outbound connection to the FL server through a proxy or gateway would make this approach practical. \n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NVIDIA/NVFlare/issues/comments/4992571484/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"hear